# KEYMAP.md §Global (Normal mode, all Hub screens) [A22] — `H` collapses / expands the repos
# rail (240 ↔ 44 px icon rail)
#
# `H` is the one Hub affordance whose whole effect is geometry: `docs/TESTING-HARNESS.md` §3
# makes the rail's own width the collapse oracle, because the rail has no control to name and
# nothing else in the snapshot moves. That width is in the snapshot — `repos.rail` drops from
# 240 to 44 in `targets` — but no predicate can read it, because a target name contains the `.`
# a dotted path splits on. So the collapse is evidenced by the screenshot, and asserted here as
# what a collapse must *preserve*: the rail keeps its rows, its selection and its focus on both
# sides of the toggle, and still navigates while it is an icon strip.
fixture: busy
await idle 30000
key g r
await hub_pane == Repos
assert focused == repos.row[0] && lists.repos.rows[2] exists
key j
await focused == repos.row[1]
dump expanded

# Collapsed, the rail is an icon strip: same rows, same cursor, same key context.
key H
await idle
assert hub_pane == Repos && focused == repos.row[1] && key_contexts[1] == Repos
assert lists.repos.rows[2] exists && lists.repos.selected.label == "acme/api"
shot collapsed
dump collapsed

# A collapsed rail still navigates ...
key j
await focused == repos.row[2]
assert lists.repos.selected.label == "acme/web"

# ... and `H` expands it again with the cursor untouched.
key H
await idle
assert hub_pane == Repos && focused == repos.row[2] && lists.repos.selected.label == "acme/web"
dump expanded-again
quit
